# .public-cloud — this repo is PUBLIC CLOUD and has NO PRIVATE TWIN.
#
# Read by hygiene's hy_repo_type(). Its presence is what makes this repo classify as public cloud;
# without it, a GitHub repo that no .mirror-manifest names reads as PRIVATE CLOUD, which is the
# right fail-closed default for a mirror and the wrong answer for this one. The effect of getting
# it wrong was silent: every save ran Set G, the unpublished-GitHub gate, on a world-readable repo.
#
# ⚠️ A REASON IS MANDATORY. An empty marker is not a decision, same rule as .no-backup.

REASON  Born public. There is no private repo behind this one: it was created as a public
        Vercel-deployed project on 2026-08-06, not curated out of private work. So there is no
        .mirror-manifest, nothing to derive an allowlist from, and no twin to save first.

# 🔒 WHAT THIS COSTS, STATED PLAINLY, BECAUSE IT IS LESS PROTECTION THAN A MIRROR GETS.
#
# A mirror publishes a SUBSET: a manifest names every file on both sides, a derived allowlist is
# enforced by pre-push, and deny patterns in the private twin back it up. None of that exists here,
# and none of it can, because all three are derived from a private side.
#
# So for this repo:
#   • Everything committed publishes. There is no "not for publication" path.
#   • Set A is the only MECHANICAL guard on content — secrets, file size and kind, identity.
#   • Set B's judgement half is entirely human: G1-G5 asked at the world-readable bar, every save.
#
# ▶ If this ever needs to hold something back, that is the signal to give it a private twin and
#   demote this repo to a real mirror, not to add exceptions here.
